DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     A test suite is a collection of test programs and is represented by a hi‐
     erarchical layout of test binaries on the file system.  Any subtree of
     the file system can represent a test suite, provided that it includes one
     or more KKyyuuaaffiillees, which are the test suite definition files.

     A KKyyuuaaffiillee is a Lua script whose purpose is to describe the structure of
     the test suite it belongs to.  To do so, the script has access to a col‐
     lection of special functions provided by kyua(1) as described in _H_e_l_p_e_r
     _f_u_n_c_t_i_o_n_s.

   FFiillee vveerrssiioonniinngg
     Every KKyyuuaaffiillee file starts with a call to ssyynnttaaxx(_i_n_t _v_e_r_s_i_o_n).  This call
     determines the specific schema used by the file so that future backwards-
     incompatible modifications to the file can be introduced.

     Any new KKyyuuaaffiillee file should set _v_e_r_s_i_o_n to ‘2’.

   TTeesstt ssuuiittee ddeeffiinniittiioonn
     If the KKyyuuaaffiillee registers any test programs, the KKyyuuaaffiillee must define the
     name of the test suite the test programs belong to by using the
     tteesstt__ssuuiittee() function at the very beginning of the file.

     The test suite name provided in the tteesstt__ssuuiittee() call tells kyua(1) which
     set of configuration variables from kyua.conf(5) to pass to the test pro‐
     grams at run time.

